   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "KOSPI falls 6% as fears over US data-centre limits hit chip stocks",
   "when": "Fri 6 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI closed at 5,059.69, down 6.02%, after touching a low about 8.8% below the previous close. A circuit breaker and a sell-sidecar were triggered early in the session. SK hynix closed down 10.44% and Samsung Electronics down 6.35%. Foreign investors sold a net 2.77 trillion won. The won weakened to about 1,357 per dollar. Korean press ties the fall to worries that the Democratic midterm win could slow US AI data-centre building.",
